## Fitness for purpose (round-4 producer, plan §5 `paired_compare.py`)

From a run directory alone the producer can, without trusting the run's claims: hash `eval_manifest.json` and compare with `completion.eval_manifest_sha256`; hash both outputs against `completion.outputs`; read `meta.eval_manifest_sha256` from both outputs and compare; take from the manifest `checkpoint_sha256` (re-hash the checkpoint), `manifest_hash` / `manifest_file_sha256` / `manifest_seed` (re-hash the reference manifest), `gl_seed`, `num_shot`, `yaw_cols` / `acoustic_cols` / `e_acoustic_cols`, `conditions`, `batch_size` / `batch_canonical` / `tf32`, `max_samples` / `n_samples` / `split_count`, `data_identity.inventory_sha256` (recomputable with `data_identity`), and `evaluator_closure` (paths + `reviewed_blob_sha256` → the digest is recomputable from git alone at `reviewed_commit`, independent of the working tree) plus `source_closures.{entrypoint,writer}`; compare the digests with the profile's approved values. Missing or weak for that purpose: (i) `reviewed_commit` may be a short or symbolic ref (finding 2) — the producer must resolve it before `git show`; (ii) no `schema_version` on the manifest or completion (the profiles carry one; add `manifest_schema: 1` / `completion_schema: 1`); (iii) no timestamps in the completion (`started_at` = the log stem, `finalised_at`) and no exit status / revalidation record — the log name is the only start time, as in exp_03; (iv) the training-side bindings of plan §4 (finding 5); (v) the completion does not list the run directory's contents (finding 4). None of these blocks round 4 from being written against the current layout; (i) and (iv) should be settled before the confirmatory evaluations are launched.

